# When pytest sees a conftest.py file, it treats the directory containing it as the root of a package hierarchy and automatically handles the pathing for you. This means that you can import modules from the parent directory without needing to modify sys.path or use relative imports. The conftest.py file is used to define fixtures and other test configurations that can be shared across multiple test files in the same directory or subdirectories. By placing the fixture in conftest.py, you can easily reuse it in any test file within that directory structure without worrying about import paths.